  "description": "The Backroad Unsupported is an adventure gravel bike with carbon frame that puts the focus on comfort, versatility and cargo capacity. Thanks to features such as the generous tyre clearance of 53 mm, a frame compartment, detachable frame bags, dynamo lighting and a USB-C port under the handlebar, it is the perfect companion for long tours in versatile terrain or bikepacking. Characteristics and advantages: The Backroad Unsupported weight about 11.0 kg1 and – thanks to dynamo lighting and integrated power bank – is perfectly equipped for long bikepacking tours and ultra-distance races. The Unsupported model features wider 50 mm tyres and the mechanical Shimano GRX RX820 1x12 groupset with a 40-tooth chainring up front and a 10–51-tooth cassette at the rear. This way, the shifting system remains independent from power, is easy to maintain and to repair, if necessary. The wide gear range with a light mountain gear even tackles long, steep climbs when carrying luggage. + Integrated lighting and power supply + Light mountain gear and comfortable tyres + Ideal for bikepacking and long distances Ideal for: • anyone looking for an adventure gravel bike for bikepacking with lighting and power supply • multi-day bikepacking tours and ultra-distances • self-supported races and long-distance rides with a focus on maximum comfort • riders who want to power their lights, navigation and devices independently while riding • extended gravel adventures with luggage on changing terrain Less suitable for: • pure gravel racing with a focus on minimum weight and aerodynamics • short, quick after-work rides without a focus on long distances • technically challenging MTB trails or tough off-road riding Highlights: • SON 29 S hub dynamo – sleek and efficient, for high-end power generatio • Supernova lighting – bright illumination up to 1000 lumens incl. rear light and high beam • USB-C charging port – power supply for devices directly on the handlebar, with integrated K-Werk buffer battery • Power switch on the handlebar – easy switching between power for the lights and charging of the power bank • Magnetic Fidlock bag system – including a frame bag (approx. 3 litres) and top tube bag (approx. 0.7 litres) • Integrated frame compartment – – space for tools and equipment, including a tool bag • 18 attachment points – flexible mounting of bottles, bags and other accessories • Tyre clearance up to 53 mm – – comfort and grip on rough terrain • Carbon seat post with a low clamp – comfort through flex Other features: The Backroad Unsupported comes with Shimano's mechanical 1x12 GRX RX820 gravel top groupset, extra wide 50 mm Schwalbe G-One Overland tyres, robust Rose G30 aluminium wheels (27 mm rim width) and a chainguide to protect against chain drops. The fi´zi:k Terra Argo X7 saddle ensures a sporty level of comfort. The Rose handlebar and stem also allow for attachment of additional parts such as an aerobar or a computer mount. Note: Pedals are not included. ¹ may vary up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, reference frame colour dune, size M/L, without pedals and bags.",
